  "comments": [
    {"at":0,"placement":"line","text":"Gives in A the pixel value (0-3) for current_colour in the cell of pixel_ptr. 0 = the background colour. Loads the cell colours (load_cell_colours), then continues at colour_slot_in_cell. Also an entry of the JMP table at $0900."},
    {"at":12,"placement":"line","text":"Gives in A the pixel value (1-3) of the cell colour (cell_colour_1-3) that is current_colour. When no cell colour is current_colour, counts the pixels of each value in the 8 bytes of the cell. The value with the fewest pixels (the higher value when equal) gets current_colour in the screen or colour RAM (write_cell_colours), and A gives this value."},
    {"at":43,"placement":"side","text":"work_ptr = first bitmap byte of the cell."},
    {"at":146,"placement":"line","text":"Sets cell_screen_ptr and cell_colour_ptr for the cell of the selected pixel (bitmap_row_base, pixel_x) and reads the cell colours into cell_colour_1-3 (read_cell_colours). Does nothing when the cell is the cell of the last load (cached_cell_ptr)."},
    {"at":163,"placement":"side","text":"(bitmap_row_base - $6000) / 8 = row * 40."},
    {"at":185,"placement":"side","text":"+ pixel_x / 4: the column of the cell."},
    {"at":200,"placement":"side","text":"Screen at $5c00."},
    {"at":208,"placement":"side","text":"$5c + $7c = $d8: the page of colour RAM."},
    {"at":212,"placement":"line","text":"Reads the colours of the cell at cell_screen_ptr and cell_colour_ptr: cell_colour_1 = high nybble of the screen byte, cell_colour_2 = low nybble, cell_colour_3 = colour RAM. Then stores pixel_ptr AND $f8 in cached_cell_ptr."},
    {"at":247,"placement":"line","text":"Writes cell_colour_1 (high nybble) and cell_colour_2 (low nybble) to the screen byte at cell_screen_ptr, and cell_colour_3 to the colour RAM at cell_colour_ptr."}
  ],
